---
import captures from "../data/captures.json";
const entry = captures.commands.explain;
---

<section
  class="section wrap terminal-section"
  aria-labelledby="terminal-heading"
>
  <div class="terminal-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">04 / THE ACTUAL CLI</p><h2 id="terminal-heading">
      Answers where<br />you work.
    </h2><p>
      No account. No dashboard to maintain.<br />A report in the terminal you
      already have.
    </p><a
      class="text-link"
      href="https://github.com/ob4cl/configlens/blob/main/docs/getting-started.md"
      >Read the getting-started guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    ><p class="small muted">
      Captured from {captures.binaryVersion} against isolated synthetic files. No
      command on this page executes.
    </p>
  </div><div class="terminal">
    <div class="terminal-top">
      <span class="terminal-dots" aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span><span
        >configlens / synthetic sandbox</span
      ><span class="tiny-label">READ ONLY PREVIEW</span>
    </div><div class="command-tabs" aria-label="Captured command">
      {
        ["explain", "clients", "scan", "doctor", "snapshot", "diff"].map(
          (name) => (
            <button data-command={name} aria-pressed={name === "explain"}>
              {name}
            </button>
          ),
        )
      }
    </div><div class="terminal-command">
      <code id="terminal-command">$ {entry.command}</code><button
        id="copy-command"
        class="copy-button"
        aria-label="Copy displayed CLI command">Copy</button
      >
    </div><pre
      id="terminal-output"
      tabindex="0"
      aria-label="Captured command output">{entry.stdout}{entry.stderr && `
[stderr]
${entry.stderr}`}</pre><div
      class="terminal-footer"
    >
      <span id="terminal-exit">EXIT {entry.exitCode} · FULL OUTPUT</span><span
        id="copy-status"
        role="status"></span>
    </div>
  </div><p class="section-caption terminal-caption">
    Output is real; paths are normalized. <code>$SANDBOX</code> replaces only the
    throwaway directory prefix. Commands retain all capture arguments; set up the
    sandbox before using them. <a
      href="https://github.com/ob4cl/configlens/blob/main/website/scripts/capture-fixtures.py"
      >Reproduce the captures ↗</a
    >
  </p>
</section>
